ENVIRONMENT DETAILS
----------------------------------------
Operating System: Ubuntu (used in both GCP VM and VirtualBox)
Platform: Google Cloud Platform (Compute Engine) and VirtualBox

----------------------------------------
STEP 1: CONNECT TO VM (GCP)
----------------------------------------
Command used:

gcloud compute ssh <INSTANCE_NAME>

----------------------------------------
STEP 2: UPDATE SYSTEM AND INSTALL PYTHON & PIP
----------------------------------------
Commands used:

sudo apt update
sudo apt upgrade -y

python3 --version

sudo apt install python3-pip -y

pip3 --version

----------------------------------------
STEP 3: INSTALL REQUIRED LIBRARIES
----------------------------------------
Commands used:

pip3 install flask
pip3 install gunicorn

----------------------------------------
STEP 4: CREATE APPLICATION FILE
----------------------------------------
Command used:

nano app.py

Code written in app.py:

from flask import Flask

app = Flask(__name__)

@app.route('/')
def home():
    return "Hello, GCP Auto Scaling using Ubuntu!"

if __name__ == "__main__":
    app.run(host='0.0.0.0', port=80)

Save and exit:
CTRL + X
Press Y
Press ENTER

----------------------------------------
STEP 5: RUN THE APPLICATION
----------------------------------------
Command used:

sudo python3 app.py

Access in browser:

http://<EXTERNAL_IP>

----------------------------------------
STEP 6: CONFIGURE FIREWALL (GCP)
----------------------------------------
Command used:

gcloud compute firewall-rules create allow-http \
--allow tcp:80 \
--source-ranges 0.0.0.0/0 \
--target-tags http-server

----------------------------------------
STEP 7: RUN APPLICATION IN BACKGROUND
----------------------------------------
Commands used:

sudo apt install screen

screen -S app

sudo python3 app.py

Detach screen session:
CTRL + A + D

----------------------------------------
STEP 8: AUTO SCALING SETUP (BASIC)
----------------------------------------
Commands used:

gcloud compute instance-templates create my-template \
--machine-type=e2-medium \
--image-family=ubuntu-2004-lts \
--image-project=ubuntu-os-cloud

gcloud compute instance-groups managed create my-group \
--base-instance-name=my-instance \
--template=my-template \
--size=2 \
--zone=us-central1-a

gcloud compute instance-groups managed set-autoscaling my-group \
--max-num-replicas=5 \
--target-cpu-utilization=0.6 \
--zone=us-central1-a

